Article 2 (Functions)
(1) The Committee shall deliberate on the following matters in response to requests for advice from the Minister of the National Court Administration:
1. Matters concerning the location of courthouse buildings;
2. Other matters relating to the implementation of courthouse construction projects that have been referred to the Committee.
(2) The Committee shall deliberate on the following matters:
1. Appropriateness of design guidelines where the design of a building, etc. is commissioned through a design competition;
2. Appropriateness of terms of reference for design services;
3. Matters specified in the following items:
(a) Where a preliminary review of a public building project plan under the main clause of Article 23 (2) of the Act, or a re-review under paragraph (4) of that Article (hereinafter referred to as a "preliminary review"), has been conducted: Matters concerning the reflection of the opinions expressed in the preliminary review;
(b) Where no preliminary review has been conducted but a feasibility study falling under any subparagraph of Article 20 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Architectural Services Industry Promotion Act has been conducted: Matters concerning the reflection of the results of the feasibility study and the appropriateness of architectural planning performed under Article 22-2 (2) of the Act;
(c) In other cases: Matters concerning the appropriateness of architectural planning performed under Article 22-2 (2) of the Act.
